te the probability of obtaining red twice and explain why the probabilities can be multiplied.","marks":4,"difficulty":3,"minutes":8,"scheme":"M1: First draw red probability \\(\\frac{3}{7}\\).\nB1: Replacement keeps the total and composition unchanged.\nB1: Multiply \\(\\frac{3}{7}\\times\\frac{3}{7}\\).\nA1: Obtain \\(\\frac{9}{49}\\).\nAnswer: \\(\\frac{9}{49}\\)"},{"id":"MG-I-EXAM-CYLSURF-2","qualification":"IGCSE","programme":"exam","exam_tier":"Core","topic":"Mensuration · Cylinders","prompt":"A closed right circular cylinder has radius \\(3\\text{ cm}\\) and height \\(5\\text{ cm}\\). Find both its exact volume and its total surface area in terms of \\(\\pi\\). Show the formulae used and give units.","marks":4,"difficulty":3,"minutes":9,"scheme":"M1: Use \\(V=\\pi r^2h\\).\nB1: Calculate volume \\(45\\pi\\text{ cm}^3\\).\nB1: Use \\(S=2\\pi r^2+2\\pi rh\\).\nA1: Calculate surface area \\(48\\pi\\text{ cm}^2\\).\nAnswer: \\(V=45\\pi\\text{ cm}^3,\\quad S=48\\pi\\text{ cm}^2\\)"},{"id":"MG-G-EXAM-PCTCHANGE-3","qualification":"GCSE","programme":"exam","exam_tier":"Foundation","topic":"Number · Successive percentage changes","prompt":"A laptop has original price \\(\\pounds 300\\). Its price increases by \\(20\\%\\), then the new price is reduced by \\(25\\%\\). Find the final price in pounds and explain why the changes must be applied successively.","marks":5,"difficulty":3,"minutes":8,"scheme":"M1: Use the increase multiplier \\(\\frac{6}{5}\\).\nB1: Find intermediate price \\(\\pounds 360\\).\nB1: Use the reduction multiplier \\(\\frac{3}{4}\\).\nB1: Obtain final price \\(\\pounds 270\\).\nA1: Explain that each percentage is of the new price.\nAnswer: \\(\\pounds 270\\)"},{"id":"MG-G-EXAM-RATIO-3","qualification":"GCSE","programme":"exam","exam_tier":"Foundation","topic":"Ratio · Sharing and interpretation","prompt":"A community group shares \\(\\pounds 54\\) between Projects A and B in the ratio \\(4:5\\). Calculate both shares. A volunteer claims that each p